From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:55:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cdp: report uncanceled window errors through Runtime

Window.reportError previously dispatched error events and only logged the
uncanceled result, leaving React recoverable errors invisible to CDP and
Playwright pageerror consumers (Sephora S01-A).

Dispatch a synchronous host exception notification after cancellation has
been decided, including the no-listener path. Snapshot inert error text in
owned storage across reentrant listeners, retain the original value and
native stack, and report nested listener/onerror failures without recursive
window event dispatch. Do not read page-controlled diagnostic getters.

Subscribe each attached Runtime session independently and wrap the original
value in its originating context on that session. Use negative host IDs to
avoid V8 exception-ID collisions and the console object group so diagnostic
clear commands release the handles. Serialize native stack frames and enable
bounded native stack capture in release builds as well as Debug.

Keep window ErrorEvent source-location correction, promise-rejection
reporting, Sephora auth readiness and basket functionality outside this fix.

Validated with the existing 1,658 upstream tests and temporary CDP/Playwright
controls for cancellation, recursive errors, arbitrary values, inert getters,
multiple sessions, contexts, handle cleanup and reentrant message lifetime.
No new upstream tests are added.
